From: Kyle Hsiao <kylehsiao@google.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 19:20:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix out-of-bounds write in stpropnci_process_std

An out-of-bounds write vulnerability exists in the ST NFC HAL when processing `RF_NFCEE_DISCOVERY_REQ_NTF` messages from the NFC controller. The `stpropnci_process_std()` function trusted the chip-provided entry count without bounds-checking against the fixed-size `ee_info` array, which could be exploited by a compromised NFC controller to overwrite adjacent global state data.

This commit addresses the issue by adding:
1. A check to ensure `payloadlen` is sufficient for the number of entries claimed by the payload.
2. A bounds check to prevent `stpropnci_state.nb_ee_info` from exceeding the capacity of the `ee_info` array before assigning a new `nfcee_id`.
3. A similar bounds check for `stpropnci_state.nb_active_nfcees` in the `NFCEE_MODE_SET_NTF` block to ensure it does not write past the bounds of the `active_nfcee_ids` array.

Test: m libstpropnci-vendor

Bug: 522376080
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX
